## 4. Eligibility (re-assessed at each origin)
${or(s.eligibility, DEF.eligibility)}

Every nested trial is itself a **new-user trial started at that origin**, so the same windows as an active-comparator new-user design are applied at *each* origin, all measured **before** that origin: a **new-user washout of ${daysTxt(s.washout)}** with no prior exposure or comparator, and a **covariate / eligibility look-back of ${covLbText(s)}**. Because these windows move with the origin, eligibility, treatment assignment and the start of follow-up remain aligned at every trial's time zero — which is what prevents immortal-time bias. A patient who is ineligible at one origin (for example, still inside the washout) may become eligible at a later one.

## 5. Time zero and treatment assignment
