## 6. Enrolment across trials
${or(s.multiple, DEF.multiple)}

${REUSE}

## 7. Confounding adjustment
${or(s.confounding, DEF.confounding)}

Covariates are re-measured at **each** origin, over the look-back windows above. A patient who enters several trials therefore carries a different covariate vector — and a different propensity score — in each. Balance (standardised mean differences) is assessed **within trial**, not only in the pooled dataset, because a pooled table can appear balanced while individual trials are not.

## 8. Follow-up and outcome
${stop(or(s.followup, DEF.followup))} Maximum follow-up per trial: **${daysTxt(s.futrial)}**. Outcome: **${or(s.outcome, "(outcome)")}**.

Trials with later origins have less calendar time remaining before the data end, so they are administratively censored earlier. Long-term contrasts are therefore informed mainly by the earliest trials; we report how many trials are still contributing at each follow-up time.

