## 9. Estimand and effect measure
The target estimand is ${estimandText(s.estimand)}. We report ${effectText(s)}.

The pooled estimate is not the effect in one population: with a single treatment coefficient across all trials it is an average of the origin-specific effects, weighted by how much information each trial contributes — and those weights are data-dependent, because later trials carry less remaining follow-up (Section 8). We report the per-trial estimates and their sizes so the average can be read for what it is.
